mantle rm268
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_vigdis_pitchmarsh
title the pocket palette
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk matches_a_street_to_a_strip_of_colour
likes mutton_stew dancing old_maps misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud cold_tea
fears forgetting_the_colour_of_clear_water
hopes to_own_a_window_above_the_smoke
topics work +0.4 travel +0.3 festival +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=close refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# matches scraps of colour to corners of the city and keeps the prettiest route a shade secret.

words
oath! = By hammer-red and sea-green | Strike me violet
saying! = Blue brings my feet home | A street wears more colours than a map admits
card = a strip of buff card | a little painted slip
blue = slate blue | the blue of a late shadow
red = red iron | brick powdered fine
yellow = a turnip yellow | butter yellow
edge = the palest edge | a washed margin
strip = my colour scrap | a swatch of linen
turn = a painted turning | one bright corner
stain = a smoky smudge | a streak of ochre
mist = a pearl of fog | low morning mist
dance = a sliding dance step | a quick heel turn
pot = the stew kettle | a fat brown pot
mud = tar-dark mud | a sticky black patch

any
opinion dole for 3 : Hunger bleaches the whole street. A bowl of hot food puts the colours back.
opinion merchants against 2 : Fancy wrapping never made me a larger supper.
opinion houses against 2 : I'd like to carry my shade card upstairs and see the colour of whoever sets my wage.
opinion strangers for 1 : Plenty of stew stretches a little further if the last bowl brings a fresh account of the road.
opinion sump for 1 : No use calling our streets all grey. Hold six greys alongside one another and look again.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Pleased to have a fresh face to remember. | Hello. There's colour in the day already.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome by my elbow. | Room on the clean side here.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Pale morning. Glad of company. | First light's good for meeting faces.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening, with the colours settling down. | Come where the light still holds.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin bring their own colours. | There's the familiar outline.
line again.open : Another turn brings you back. | Same face in a different light.
line greet.return : I heard you plainly. | Here, I've a clean paw for you.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You've brightened my corner already. | Your voice makes a comfortable shade.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Time enough while this dries. | I can listen over my work.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Mind the dark patch. | The light's nearly spent. Welcome in.
line farewell : Keep a colour for yourself. | Come back by the bright way.
line farewell.return : Find the dry side home. | May the turns come clear.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Walk where there's a lamp still burning. | Gentle night beyond my window.
line react.news : Give me the colours true. | Let me hear the plain bits first.
line react.news.new : That shades things differently. | Fresh colour to my ear.
line react.news.known : Old stain, still showing. | I recognise that particular outline.
line react.news.doubt : I'd wait until the smudge dries before deciding. | That sounds touched up to please somebody.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah, even the bright strip looks dull hearing that. | Let me take some weight.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Something worth saving a swatch of. | That's good light let in.
line ask.how : How's the day coloured you? | Any brightness in your pocket?
line answer.how : Still keeping a little blue back. | Some colour left under my nails.
line decline : I'd best keep this hour for mixing. | I reckon my feet need a quiet turning.
line accept_decline : Then we'll let that colour dry. | Your own shade suits you best.
line thank : I'll keep that kindness bright. | That's a fine colour you've left me.
line sympathise : Share my dry edge awhile. | I'm beside you through the dull bit.
line reassure : There'll be a kinder shade somewhere. | I've room to walk alongside.
line preclose : I must put these slips in order. | Best catch my turning now.

scene grey
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have six greys for one street. | One street's worth a whole pocket of swatches.
b : Which grey is home? | What separates the shades?
a : Warmest one where the shutters close. | Rub the dust off. Each corner keeps its own light.

scene forge
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I swear in colours at work.
b : What colours? | When things go wrong?
a : Iron red for temper, green for relief. | If the batch comes right I save the blue for later.

scene rise
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like an upstairs window with nothing smoking in front.
b : What sight would you want? | Facing where?
a : The true colour of a white shirt hung out to dry. | East enough for the pale part of morning.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The mist takes all my best colours out walking.
b : Even the red? | Does it bring them back?
a : Red goes a pink so thin you can see through it. | Every roof gives a little back as it lifts.

scene step
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I learn a dance by looking at shoes.
b : What about the tune? | Whose shoes?
a : That's what keeps my ears employed. | The pair that look as if the wearer has forgotten about them.

scene wrong
when topic=travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wrong road on a map can still lead somewhere fine.
b : Would you follow it? | What if it stops short?
a : If I have daylight and a heel of supper. | I'd give the blank a colour of my own.

scene kettle
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the stew's nearly ready by the fat on top.
b : What colour? | Before you smell it?
a : Little gold islands, splitting and meeting again. | I've generally smelt it so long my nose has stopped paying attention.

scene tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea makes a fair wash for a map.
b : Wouldn't you drink it? | Which bit of the map?
a : I've more use for the colour than the taste. | The road I don't particularly want anybody finding.

scene heel
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In thick mud I put my heels where another wolf's already been.
b : To save your shoes? | Can you match every stride?
a : To save my temper. Those dark spatters travel high. | Sometimes I have to dance to do it.

scene band
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I keep a clean strip under my cuff.
b : To test the colours? | Does the strip stay white?
a : It tells me how far the dust has travelled. | Just the middle. The edges make a map of my work.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd pick something a touch warmer than blue for #self.friend#.
b : Why warmer? | Would you say which?
a : Blue's a friend seen over a shoulder. I want a face looking back. | I'd hold up the card first. A friend has a say.

scene tour
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll mark a turning in colour for a newcomer.
b : And if the paint runs? | What marks home?
a : I can show it on foot. That's the honest map. | Whatever colour the gate looks coming back tired.

scene night
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Under a little lamp my reds begin to tell lies.
b : Does the lamp fool you? | What do you do?
a : Never quite the same lie twice. That's the trouble. | Sleep on a choice that has to look good in daylight.

scene price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll turn cloth over before I offer coin.
b : To look for fraying? | What catches your eye?
a : To see how much colour ever made it through. | The inner fold that never saw sunlight. It knows the original price.

scene warmth
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's always a warm patch on my imaginary map.
b : A hearth? | For bad weather?
a : Could be the shape of a welcome on a threshold. | Especially for a day when the light shows up every hole in my coat.

scene hands
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My fingers keep little crescents of yesterday's colour.
b : Can you wash them off? | What's there now?
a : Eventually. For two or three mornings I get reminded where I've been. | Something dark as the back of my eyelid. There's been a fair bit of work.

scene secret
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I might lend you my best map without the final turning.
b : What are you keeping? | Couldn't I guess?
a : A patch of open sky I still have to myself. | Perhaps. I'd like the trouble of being found.

scene carts
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon puts a blank in my working colours.
b : How do you fill it? | White, then?
a : Use a little of the colours still here and promise less. | A blank can be any colour I've used up.

story green [topic=memories]
  : I once painted a neat green path across a scrap of wrapping paper and followed it for half a morning.
  : I arrived at the very door where I'd begun, with the paper held sideways the whole time.
  b : Did you repaint it?
  : I wrote my own door at both ends. A proper circular walk.

story hem [topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing]
  : I pinned a blue strip to my hem, thinking I'd watch the steps through a tune I'd never danced.
  : A hem turns faster than an eye. All I could follow was the one blue streak.
  b : Did you keep your footing?
  : I looked up at a face instead. The feet managed without my help.

story lid [topic=food]
  : Once my pot lid took a strange purple stain. I scrubbed it until I could see my own nose.
  : The purple turned up next morning just as deep. I pulled the blind across and it vanished.
  b : What had it been?
  : Early light travelling through a bit of coloured glass. I gave up polishing my breakfast.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Keep the clean margin under the cuff. | Dark swatch before the pale one.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=dancing
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Half turn, touch heels. There's the bright step. | Plenty of tune left in these shoes.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold the swatch where morning finds it. | Pale enough light to see a thin wash.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Cold in the cup means brown for the map. | Might as well dip a brush now.

dlg resident.hub : Let me see your face in the good light. There, I'll know it again.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a face worth saving the right colour for.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter self.workplace] : I get colour on my cuffs at #self.workplace# and carry some of it home on purpose.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's the plain outline. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Take the way that gives you something worth looking at.

graft resident.hub
choice How can a piece of cloth give directions? -> cloth_road
node cloth_road
say There's a red wall with a blue shadow under it, and a turn where the air goes amber from a lamp. Fold three coloured bits together and that's my way home.
free
choice Does anyone else find the same way? -> cloth_shift
choice I've got the red wall. -> hub
node cloth_shift
say Not after the light changes. That's when a little local company comes in handy. I've no objection to delaying the walk by a cup or two.
choice I'll remember to ask you. -> hub
choice I'll see what colour the road is now. -> bye
